  "description": "Vendor-neutral contract for OutWit language-model providers: IIntelligenceProvider sends one structured request (instructions, content, answer schema, output limit) and returns the answer with its stop category and token usage, or a categorized failure that carries no vendor text and no credential. A provider is made per connection (base URL, model, retries, timeout) with the key supplied per request, so one host can serve many keys. Providers ship as separate OutWit.Shared.Intelligence.Provider.* packages, each a plugin that registers its IIntelligenceProviderFactory.",
